# Inkling-2-Mini HI2 3.5 bpw (quant_method rdna_hint_flex, quantizer
# rdna-hint-flex-quantizer-inkling feat/inkling2-source) on TWO gfx1030 cards (V620,
# 29.98 GiB each), TP=2.  Routed experts INT2/INT4 in the HI2 format; attention,
# embeddings, router, norms, loop controllers and the vision tower bf16.  Language
# model only for now (no DSpark, no vision); FULL_AND_PIECEWISE HIP graphs, one-shot
# HIP all-reduce (rdna_ar), prefix caching.
#
# UNRUN as of 2026-11-24: every GPU was leased.  The CPU gates and the serve-dir
# preparation are done (tools/inkling_hi2/README.md sections 1-2, docs/rdna2/
# inkling2-hi2-runtime-receipt.md); the first GPU step is the kernel test of
# section 2.1, then this recipe.
#
#   bash tools/rdna/serve_rdna.sh RECIPE=inkling2-hi2-tp2 \
#     MODEL=~/w4a8_runs/inkling-hi2-runtime/serve-bpw3.5 \
#     VENV=/path/to/venv HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1
#   PRINT=1 bash tools/rdna/serve_rdna.sh RECIPE=inkling2-hi2-tp2 MODEL=... \
#     VENV=... HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1   # assemble only, CPU
#
# The model directory is the quantizer's output plus the symlinks of
# tools/inkling_hi2/prep_serve_dir.sh (config.json, index, both shards, tokenizer,
# stock mtp.safetensors).  The loader takes the expert format from config.json's
# quantization_config; no extra switch selects HI2.
#
# Memory, header census of the real 3.5 bpw output (tools/inkling_hi2/validate_dir.py,
# 2026-11-24): experts 10.08 GiB, dense 3.59 GiB, vision 0.59 GiB, MTP 0.59 GiB,
# indexed total 13.67 GiB.  Per rank at TP=2: experts 5.04 GiB + dense (8.02 GiB when
# sharded .. 9.81 GiB replicated) = 8.02-9.81 GiB before KV; a V620 has 29.98 GiB.
# MAXLEN/KV is the mini recipe's plain-decoding context; the HI2 KV is the same
# (16 full-attention layers, 4 KV heads / TP 2, head_dim 256, fp16 = 32 KiB/token).
# Fill KV in after the first boot logs the measured weights; no recipe number here
# has been measured with HI2 experts.

SERVE_ENTRY=cli
SERVED_NAME=inkling2-hi2
PORT=18225
TP=2
HOST=127.0.0.1
# a2 lease (HIP 0,1; PCI d1 d4).  A caller value (serve.sh passes the slot's pair)
# wins; this is the default for a direct serve_rdna.sh invocation.
HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1

MTP=0
ATTN=none
EAGER=0
CG_MODE=FULL_AND_PIECEWISE
CG_CAPTURE_SIZES=0
MAXLEN=1048576
MAXBAT=320
SEQS=8
KV=auto
GMEM=0.92
RDNA_AR=1
FEATURES="prefix-caching language-model-only"
EXTRA_ARGS='--limit-mm-per-prompt {"image":0}'

# --- RDNA vLLM env block (same as inkling2-mini-tp2) ---
TUNABLEOP=0
VLLM_KV_CACHE_MARGIN_FLOOR_MIB=2048
VLLM_FORCE_CUSTOM_ALL_REDUCE=0
VLLM_RDNA_AR_MAX_KB=256
VLLM_RDNA_AR_ONESHOT_KB=256
OMP_NUM_THREADS=8
TOKENIZERS_PARALLELISM=false
PYTHONFAULTHANDLER=1
# If the first boot fails in HIP graph capture of the HI2 serving path, rerun with
# EAGER=1 on the command line and report it (FULL_AND_PIECEWISE stays the target).
